[0.095, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[7G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m  \u001b[10G +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mto\u001b[15Gnames\u001b[21Ga\u001b[23Glater\u001b[29Gregistration\u001b[42Gcould\u001b[48Gmove.\u001b[54G**Done**\u001b[63G2026-11-25:\u001b[75Gthey\u001b[80Greturn\u001b[87Gcopies.\u001b[95G|\u001b[97GMet:\u001b[102Gthe\u001b[106G`sim`\u001b[112Gsu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mite's service case compares copies. |                                                                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 416 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m| A server's last messages delivered | Stage 5 review | Destroying a server closes every connection at\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m once, so the replies of a clean stop's last step were dropped. **Done** 2026-11-25: `Server::Closing`\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, polled after closing each session until its client has acknowledged what it was sent. | Met: the `ne\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt` suite sends a session a message, closes it, polls until it is no longer closing, and its client has\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m the message and the reason. |                                                                        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 417 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m| One XDG directory resolved alone | Stage 5 review | `ResolvePaths` resolves all four directories, so\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m a program writing only configuration needed HOME or every XDG variable. **Done** 2026-11-25: `Resolve\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mPath`, one directory, needing HOME only when i