[0.257, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest/docs/history.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 139 \u001b[22m variable or HOME (Jettison's `ResolvePath`, one directory at a time); and no test cut a snapshot's\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 140 \u001b[22m write or its catalogue's off, which the `host` suite now does. Round 2 found each resolved and one\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 141 \u001b[22m more: provisioning made a principal whose ID was past that bound, so it could never act, and now\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 142 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mrefuses it as malformed.                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 142 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mrefuses it as malformed. Round 3, aimed at what the first two had not examined, found F7 resolved and \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 143 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtwo more: making a default place's directories chmodded an existing parent named through `new/..`,    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 144 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mnow normalised first; and one long `Advance` flushed and snapshotted once at its end, now at each     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 145 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mstep due on the way, as the journal suite's long advance against short ones shows.                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 146 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 147 \u001b[22m ## R09: St\u001b[23Gge\u001b[26G5 closed — 2026-11-25\u001b[48G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[2m 148 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BMaking \u001b