[0.384, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 490 \u001b[22m reviewer attacks those claims. A reply answers each finding by number: fixed, and what proves it,\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 491 \u001b[22m or disputed, with the evidence. Round 2 shows the reviewer what changed since round 1, and it marks\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 492 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242meach earlier finding resolved, open or withdrawn. \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mTwo\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m rounds at most, then what is still open goes    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 493 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mto the user. The script exits 0 for `approve`, 1 for `changes`.                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 492 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242meach earlier finding resolved, open or withdrawn. \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mThree\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m rounds at most, then what is still open goes  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 493 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mto the user.                                                                                          \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m49\u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 495 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mA review runs when a stage of work closes, over that stage's commits, not after each task. When a     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 496 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mmajor stage of development closes, a review of the whole codebase follows: Jettison's first, then     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 497 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mManifest's, each brief aimed at what cuts across stages (determinism and replay, save compatibility,  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 498 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtrust boundaries, files and permissions, the documents against the code), since a sta