state hashes did not move.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe F8/F10 fix:\u001b[22m directories\u001b[33Gare now\u001b[41Gcreated\u001b[49Gone\u001b[53Gcomponent\u001b[63Gat\u001b[66Ga\u001b[68Gtime,\u001b[74Geach\u001b[79Gmade\u001b[84Gprivate\u001b[92Gthrough\u001b[100Gthe\u001b[104Gsame\u001b[109Gpath\u001b[114Git\u001b[117Gwas\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gcreated by. That covers \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mnew/..\u001b[39m paths and symlinks, and the world and\u001b[74Gb\u001b[77Gkup \u001b[82Girectori\u001b[91Gs use it\u001b[101Goo. A side effect:\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bwh\u001b[8Gn a world or backup directory's parent fo\u001b[50Gder\u001b[54G are missing, those\u001b[74Gp\u001b[76Grents a\u001b[85G n\u001b[88Gw creat\u001b[96Gd private a\u001b[108G w\u001b[111Gll, where\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bbefore\u001b[12Gonly the\u001b[21Gl\u001b[23Gst one was.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mYour new review rule\u001b[24G\u001b[22mis\u001b[27Gin\u001b[30GJettison\u001b[39G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mc2be3ac\u001b[39m,\u001b[48Gnot\u001b[52Gyet\u001b[56Gpushed.\u001b[64G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcross-review.sh\u001b[80G\u001b[39mnow\u001b[84Gdefaults\u001b[93Gto\u001b[96Gthree\u001b[102Grounds.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/build-and-gates.md\u001b[27G\u001b[39mnow says to\u001b[39Greview a\u001b[48Gstage's\u001b[56Gcommits\u001b[64Gwhen it closes.\u001b[80GWhen a major\u001b[93Gstage closes, a\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwhole-codebase review follow\u001b[32G, Je\u001b[37Gtison first, th\u001b[53Gn Manifest, aimed at concerns th\u001b[86Gt cut across\u001b[99Gstag\u001b[105G.\u001b[107GThe\u001b[111Gmemory\u001b[118Gis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bupdated too. I\u001b[20Gad \"major stage\" as \u001b[42Ge of \u001b[76G; tell\u001b[83Gme if you mean something larg\u001b[113Gr.\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
