[0.150, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m t` suite sends a session a message, closes it, polls until it is no longer closing, and its client has\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m  the message and the reason. |\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 417 \u001b[22m | One XDG directory resolved alone | Stage 5 review | `ResolvePaths` resolves all four directories, so\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m  a program writing only configuration needed HOME or every XDG variable. **Done** 2026-11-25: `Resolve\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m Path`, one directory, needing HOME only when its own variable is not absolute. | Met: the `platform` s\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m uite resolves configuration from its variable alone and refuses the cache with neither. |\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m418\u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m|\u001b[14GA directory made private from the start | Stage 5 review | `CreateDirectoriesDurably` made a directo\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mry with the default mode, so a caller changed it afterwards, and a flush that failed between the two l\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242meft it as made, open to everyone, and taken as already there on the next run. **Done** 2026-11-25: it \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtakes the permissions to make each directory with, under the umask, the default every permission as be\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mfore.\u001b[18G|\u001b[20GMet:\u001b[25Gthe\u001b[29G`core`\u001b[36Gsuite\u001b[42Gmakes\u001b[48Gtwo\u001b[52Gdirectories\u001b[64G0700\u001b[69Gunder\u001b[75Gone\u001b[79Gleft\u001b[84G0750,\u001b[90Gand\u001b[94Gthrough\u001b[102G`new/..`\u001b[111Gmak\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m   \u001b[12G\u001b[38;2;248;248;24